      "receiptText": "Cornish Potato Cake\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cb\u003EIngredients\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nBoiled potatoes 6\u003Cbr\u003E\nflour 1\u00BD lb.\u003Cbr\u003E\ndripping \u00BD lb.\u003Cbr\u003E\ncurrants \u00BD lb.\u003Cbr\u003E\negg 1\u003Cbr\u003E\nmilk \u00BC pint (4 oz.)\u003Cbr\u003E\ncream of tartar 1 teaspoonful\u003Cbr\u003E\nbicarbonate soda \u00BD teaspoonful.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cb\u003EMethod\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nRub the dripping into the flour.\u003Cbr\u003E\nAdd the rest of the dry ingredients and mix well.\u003Cbr\u003E\nMash the potatoes and mix them in.\u003Cbr\u003E\nMake into a dough with the egg and milk.\u003Cbr\u003E\nRoll out one inch thick and bake till brown.\u003Cbr\u003E"
